# ============================================================
#  Keep private things out of the public repo.
#
#  GitHub Pages needs a public repository on the free plan, so
#  the whole app is readable by anyone who finds it. That's fine
#  for the code — the key in config.js is meant to be public and
#  the database rules mean nobody can read your data without your
#  email and password.
#
#  What is NOT fine in public is your actual work: job names,
#  clients, hours. None of the files below are needed to run the
#  app, so they stay on your computer.
# ============================================================

# Your task tracker history — every job name and hour you've logged
supabase/04_seed_timelog.sql
Reference/

# Development only. seed-time.js and the tests carry the same history.
tools/

# Generated previews
preview.html
preview-test.html
preview-debug.html
